    <span class="section-label">Check it yourself</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="max-width:30ch">Two ways to check the math against your business</h2>

    <p style="max-width:72ch">Your business may do better or worse than the example. Two free steps will tell you:</p>

    <ol class="roi-verify">
      <li>
        <div>
          <strong>Run your site through Google's speed test.</strong>
          <p>Go to <a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">pagespeed.web.dev</a>, paste your site's address, and click Analyze. Check the phone score; the computer score is usually higher and tells you less. Below 80, speed is holding your site back, and the math above roughly applies to you.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <strong>Search for your main service and city on a phone, away from your business address.</strong>
          <p>If your business appears in the local pack (the three listings with the map), local search is mostly working. If not, or only after scrolling, it's almost certainly your biggest opportunity.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

